### What happens?

`DuckDBVector` objects from a closed result set might return random values between GC calls.

After some investigation, I suspect direct buffers to be the culprit:

https://github.com/duckdb/duckdb/blob/e807b416e8885a5cb530d17e180cff88ab7fbc2a/tools/jdbc/src/jni/duckdb_java.cpp#L766-L768

Original ticket: https://github.com/dbeaver/dbeaver/issues/21598

### To Reproduce

```java
try (Connection connection = DriverManager.getConnection("jdbc:duckdb:")) {
    try (Statement statement = connection.createStatement()) {
        final Object object;

        try (ResultSet resultSet = statement.executeQuery("select {'x': 0.1, 'y': 0.2, 'z': 0.3}")) {
            resultSet.next();
            object = resultSet.getObject(1);
        }

        final String expected = "{x=0.1, y=0.2, z=0.3}";
        for (int i = 0; i < 10000; i++) {
            System.gc();
            final String actual = object.toString();
            if (!expected.equals(actual)) {
                throw new SQLException("expected != actual: " + expected + " != " + actual);
            }
        }
    }
}
```

