TypeScript 1.4 compiler removes end comment marker at end of file. This causes "Uncaught SyntaxError: Unexpected token ILLEGAL" in Chrome.

**Example ts code:**

```
var str = "Hello, world!";
document.body.innerHTML = str;

/*

 hello, world

*/
```

**Note** there is no new line at end of file after */

**Compiler output js:**

```
var str = "Hello, world!";
document.body.innerHTML = str;
/*

 hello, world

var str = "Hello, world!";
document.body.innerHTML = str;

/*

 hello, world

//# sourceMappingURL=helloworld.js.map
```

**Correct output after adding newline:**

```
var str = "Hello, world!";
document.body.innerHTML = str;
/*

 hello, world

*/
//# sourceMappingURL=helloworld.js.map
```

