## 🔍 Search Terms
extend class interface prototype declare

## ⭐ Suggestion
I don't know if there is a reason for it, but it would be nice if Typescript doesn't show methods on classes from declarations not imported.
Here `point.transform()` should not be available until we load the file containing the declaration in the project.
For backwards compatibility I would expect a compiler flag is needed for the more stricter behavior.
**Remark:** This can still cause a runtime error if the `Point.prototype.transform` is not available.

