# Bug Report

```
  class MenuItem {
    constructor(public name: string) {}
  }
```

Compiling this with `-t ESNext` produces:
```
class MenuItem {
    name;
    constructor(name) {
        this.name = name;
    }
}
```
The name field above also confuses some next stage build tools that don't support class fields yet, e.g. the popular acorn that is used by Svelte compiler (https://github.com/sveltejs/svelte/issues/6592)


However, compiling with `-t ES2021` produces more compact code without useless field declaration:
```
class MenuItem {
    constructor(name) {
        this.name = name;
    }
}
```

