Use case:

I have an abstraction over the angular 1.x API using more typescript-style classes until 2.x is popular enough to be used in the wild. As part of this, I have a base directive abstraction which simplifies the angular API. Classes then use decorators to indicate that they are angular components.

Problem:

In Typescript 1.6, the visual studio (and Typescript playground) does not properly identify subclasses for decorator calls. Instead, they give the red squiggly under it, saying that the types are not compatible, indicating some inherited member not being present on the subclass type.

Example of reproduction:

``` typescript
declare var angular: any;

class Component {
    start() {}
}

// error here, "argument typeof SomeDirective is not assignable to type Component,
// property 'start' is missing in typeof SomeDirective"
@directive('something')
class SomeDirective extends Component {

}

function directive(name: string) {
    return <T extends Component>(fn: T) => {
        angular.module('app').controller(name, fn);
    }
}
```

(and in the [playground](http://www.typescriptlang.org/Playground#src=declare%20var%20angular%3A%20any%3B%0D%0A%0D%0Aclass%20Component%20%7B%0D%0A%09apply%28%29%20%7B%7D%0D%0A%7D%0D%0A%0D%0A%40directive%28'something'%29%0D%0Aclass%20SomeDirective%20extends%20Component%20%7B%0D%0A%09%0D%0A%7D%0D%0A%0D%0Afunction%20directive%28name%3A%20string%29%20%7B%0D%0A%09return%20%3CT%20extends%20Component%3E%28fn%3A%20T%29%20%3D%3E%20%7B%0D%0A%09%09angular.module%28'app'%29.controller%28name%2C%20fn%29%3B%0D%0A%09%7D%0D%0A%7D))

Interestingly, the error is _still present_ even when the subclass _directly implements_ whatever the parent class has:

``` typescript
declare var angular: any;

class Component {
    start() {}
}

// error here, "argument typeof SomeDirective is not assignable to type Component,
// property 'start' is missing in typeof SomeDirective"
@directive('something')
class SomeDirective extends Component {
    start() {}
}

function directive(name: string) {
    return <T extends Component>(fn: T) => {
        angular.module('app').controller(name, fn);
    }
}
```

(and in the [playground](http://www.typescriptlang.org/Playground#src=declare%20var%20angular%3A%20any%3B%0D%0A%0D%0Aclass%20Component%20%7B%0D%0A%09start%28%29%20%7B%7D%0D%0A%7D%0D%0A%0D%0A%40directive%28'something'%29%0D%0Aclass%20SomeDirective%20extends%20Component%20%7B%0D%0A%09start%28%29%20%7B%7D%0D%0A%09%0D%0A%7D%0D%0A%0D%0Afunction%20directive%28name%3A%20string%29%20%7B%0D%0A%09return%20%3CT%20extends%20Component%3E%28fn%3A%20T%29%20%3D%3E%20%7B%0D%0A%09%09angular.module%28'app'%29.controller%28name%2C%20fn%29%3B%0D%0A%09%7D%0D%0A%7D))

This error also appears to be related only to decorators, normal functions work as expected, even when the decorator is called as a normal function:

``` typescript
