When using sorted sets to store time series data, usually the score is the data's timestamp. When such data comes from ever increasing timestamps like a sensor, we're in a situation that the insertion of a new element into the sorted set will always happen at the end of the set.
If instead of starting at the head and navigate the whole skip list why not add it directly at the end, making it a O(1) operation, instead of O(log N)?

This could easily be done by a simple change to zslInsert, like:

```
if( zsl->tail->score < score ) {
    // Insert at the end of the list
}
else {
    // regular insertion algorithm
}
```

